{"reviewer_participant_id": "actor:stage1-claude-02", "reviews": [{"case_id": "case:b036fd64c647dfd93e35", "verdict": "no_demonstrated_issue_within_scope", "bounded_statement": null, "root_cause": null, "issue_class": null, "evidence_atoms": [{"description": "The stated scientific task defines the estimand as explicitly conditional on passing the prespecified signal screen, i.e. the retained subset is the target domain, not a proxy for a larger one.", "observed_value": "conditional-on-screen estimand", "source_spans": [{"path": "task.md", "start_line": 1, "end_line": 1, "quoted_text": "Build a coastal-station workflow whose scientific question is the occurrence rate conditional on passing a prespecified signal screen."}]}, {"description": "The report's declared target population is the 72 screen-passing stations, matching the conditional task, and the selected result is explicitly scoped to signal-eligible stations with denominator 72.", "observed_value": "target = 72 eligible; selected rate = 18/72 among eligible", "source_spans": [{"path": "results/report.md", "start_line": 4, "end_line": 4, "quoted_text": "Target population: 72 signal-eligible stations that passed the prespecified signal screen."}, {"path": "results/report.md", "start_line": 8, "end_line": 8, "quoted_text": "[selected-result] Among signal-eligible stations, the occurrence rate was 18/72 = 25%."}]}, {"description": "The workflow builds the selected-result string from SIGNAL_ELIGIBLE_STATIONS (72) while labeling the claim 'Among signal-eligible stations', so the code-level denominator and the code-level claim scope are the same population.", "observed_value": "SIGNAL_ELIGIBLE_STATIONS = 72 used as denominator of an eligible-scoped claim", "source_spans": [{"path": "workflow/analysis.py", "start_line": 7, "end_line": 7, "quoted_text": "SIGNAL_ELIGIBLE_STATIONS = 72"}, {"path": "workflow/analysis.py", "start_line": 18, "end_line": 18, "quoted_text": "RESULT_LINE = f'[selected-result] Among signal-eligible stations, the occurrence rate was {OCCURRENCES}/{SIGNAL_ELIGIBLE_STATIONS} = {RATE_PERCENT}%.' + LF"}]}, {"description": "The input table's own semantics separate the eligible groups from an 'outside_signal_eligible' group marked not_assessed, consistent with the eligible set being the analytic domain rather than a retention artifact hiding unobserved in-domain units.", "observed_value": "18 observed / 54 not_observed eligible; 24 outside eligible, not_assessed", "source_spans": [{"path": "inputs/data.csv", "start_line": 2, "end_line": 4, "quoted_text": "signal_eligible_occurrence,18,observed\nsignal_eligible_no_occurrence,54,not_observed\noutside_signal_eligible,24,not_assessed"}]}], "counterevidence_atoms": [{"description": "The report does name a larger 96-station scheduled network, which is the strongest textual basis for arguing that a complete domain of 96 exists and that 72 is a retained subset of it; however this line is descriptive accounting and is not attached to the selected claim.", "observed_value": "96 scheduled stations named in report", "source_spans": [{"path": "results/report.md", "start_line": 3, "end_line": 3, "quoted_text": "Scheduled network: 96 stations."}]}, {"description": "Falsification span: the accounting line states the 24 non-eligible scheduled stations were never assessed for occurrence and are outside the eligible set, so the report does not claim occurrence information about them and does not present 18/72 as a network-wide rate.", "observed_value": "24 scheduled stations outside eligible set, not assessed", "source_spans": [{"path": "results/report.md", "start_line": 5, "end_line": 5, "quoted_text": "Planned-unit accounting: 18 eligible stations with an occurrence, 54 eligible stations without an occurrence, and 24 scheduled stations outside the eligible set and not assessed for occurrence."}]}], "falsification_attempt": "I tried to demonstrate the in-scope issue by searching every visible artifact for a claim that generalizes the 18/72 rate to the full 96-station scheduled network. The only complete-domain mention is the descriptive accounting line 'Scheduled network: 96 stations.' (results/report.md L0003); the target line (L0004), the accounting line (L0005), and the selected-result line (L0008) all restrict scope to the signal-eligible set, and workflow/analysis.py L0018 hard-codes that eligible-scoped wording alongside the 72 denominator. The task itself (task.md L0001) states the estimand is conditional on passing the screen. Because the denominator population and the claimed population coincide, the retained-subset-for-complete-domain mismatch could not be demonstrated.", "cross_case_evidence_used": false, "unresolved_material_questions": [], "self_reported_confidence": "high"}, {"case_id": "case:2e26bf5ece15be03717f", "verdict": "no_demonstrated_issue_within_scope", "bounded_statement": null, "root_cause": null, "issue_class": null, "evidence_atoms": [{"description": "The task requires a rate for the entire scheduled survey network, so the complete domain is the 96 scheduled stations.", "observed_value": "complete-domain target", "source_spans": [{"path": "task.md", "start_line": 1, "end_line": 1, "quoted_text": "Using the supplied coastal-station base workflow, produce a revised selected occurrence rate for the entire scheduled survey network."}]}, {"description": "The selected result uses the complete scheduled-station count (96) as the exposure denominator, not the retained subset (72), and the preceding line states the omitted stations remain in the denominator.", "observed_value": "18/96 = 0.1875", "source_spans": [{"path": "results/report.md", "start_line": 14, "end_line": 15, "quoted_text": "Exposure denominator: all 96 scheduled stations, so the 24 omitted stations stay in the denominator and contribute zero observed occurrences.\n[selected-result] Occurrence rate over the complete scheduled network: 18 occurrences divided by 96 scheduled stations = 0.1875 (18.75 occurrences per 100 scheduled stations)."}]}, {"description": "In code, the selected-result string interpolates SCHEDULED_STATIONS (96) as the denominator, confirming the report line is produced from the complete-domain count rather than the screen-passing count.", "observed_value": "SCHEDULED_STATIONS = 96 interpolated into SELECTED_LINE", "source_spans": [{"path": "workflow/analysis.py", "start_line": 6, "end_line": 6, "quoted_text": "SCHEDULED_STATIONS = 96"}, {"path": "workflow/analysis.py", "start_line": 23, "end_line": 23, "quoted_text": "SELECTED_LINE = f'[selected-result] Occurrence rate over the complete scheduled network: {OBSERVED_OCCURRENCES} occurrences divided by {SCHEDULED_STATIONS} scheduled stations = {NETWORK_RATE_FRACTION} ({NETWORK_RATE_PERCENT} occurrences per 100 scheduled stations).' + LF"}]}, {"description": "Row-level data confirm the reported counts: all 96 rows carry scheduled=yes, omitted rows carry occurrence_flag NA, and retained rows carry 0/1; the omitted stations are genuinely scheduled units of the complete domain.", "observed_value": "scheduled=yes for both retained and omitted rows", "source_spans": [{"path": "inputs/data.csv", "start_line": 2, "end_line": 5, "quoted_text": "CS-001,North,yes,retained,none,1\nCS-002,North,yes,retained,none,0\nCS-003,North,yes,retained,none,0\nCS-004,North,yes,omitted,screen_fail_low_snr,NA"}]}], "counterevidence_atoms": [{"description": "The numerator (18) is observed only among retained stations while the denominator spans all 96, which is the strongest available basis for arguing a denominator/numerator population mismatch; the report explicitly discloses this and frames the result as a lower bound rather than an unqualified network estimate.", "observed_value": "numerator from retained subset; result declared a lower bound", "source_spans": [{"path": "results/report.md", "start_line": 11, "end_line": 11, "quoted_text": "Occurrences observed among the retained stations: 18"}, {"path": "results/report.md", "start_line": 18, "end_line": 18, "quoted_text": "The 24 omitted stations were never observed, so the complete-network rate above is a lower bound on the true network rate."}]}, {"description": "Falsification span: the report affirms that no screened-subset rate appears anywhere, ruling out a hidden 18/72 selected claim.", "observed_value": "no 72-denominator rate reported", "source_spans": [{"path": "results/report.md", "start_line": 19, "end_line": 19, "quoted_text": "No screened-subset rate is reported; every claim in this report uses the complete 96 station denominator."}]}], "falsification_attempt": "I tried to demonstrate the in-scope issue by checking whether the selected result's exposure denominator is the retained subset while the claim covers the complete domain. The selected-result line (results/report.md L0015) divides by 96 scheduled stations, the denominator line (L0014) states the 24 omitted stations remain in the denominator, and workflow/analysis.py L0023 interpolates SCHEDULED_STATIONS rather than SCREEN_PASSED_STATIONS; no 18/72 rate appears in any artifact. I also checked whether the row data contradict the 96/72/24/18 counts by scanning screen_status and occurrence_flag values across inputs/data.csv L0002-L0097, and they are consistent. The narrow retained-subset-denominator mismatch therefore could not be demonstrated.", "cross_case_evidence_used": false, "unresolved_material_questions": ["Whether the missing-at-random status of the 24 screen-omitted stations makes the complete-domain rate a valid point estimate rather than only a lower bound is a separate estimand question, outside the single in-scope issue class."], "self_reported_confidence": "high"}, {"case_id": "case:35069763f06891dba5a3", "verdict": "demonstrated_issue", "bounded_statement": "The selected result asserts an occurrence rate 'for the entire scheduled survey network' but divides the 18 occurrences by the 72 screen-retained stations rather than the 96 scheduled stations that the task and the report's own target line define as the complete domain, excluding the 24 screen-omitted scheduled stations from the exposure denominator and yielding 0.25 in place of a complete-domain denominator of 96.", "root_cause": "The screen-based retention filter propagates into the exposure denominator of a complete-domain claim: workflow/analysis.py sets both SCHEDULED_STATIONS = 96 and SCREEN_PASSED_STATIONS = 72 but interpolates SCREEN_PASSED_STATIONS into SELECTED_LINE while keeping the 'entire scheduled survey network' wording, so the denominator population (retained subset) and the claimed population (complete scheduled network) diverge with no conditional restatement of the target and no approved deviation.", "issue_class": "issue-class:retained-subset-for-complete-domain", "evidence_atoms": [{"description": "The task states the reported rate must cover the entire scheduled survey network, making the complete domain the 96 scheduled stations.", "observed_value": "complete-domain target required", "source_spans": [{"path": "task.md", "start_line": 1, "end_line": 1, "quoted_text": "Build a compact coastal-station workflow that reports one occurrence rate for the entire scheduled survey network."}]}, {"description": "The report's own target line fixes the complete domain at all 96 scheduled stations, and the accounting lines record 72 retained and 24 omitted, so the 72 is a proper subset of the stated target domain.", "observed_value": "target = 96; retained = 72; omitted = 24", "source_spans": [{"path": "results/report.md", "start_line": 4, "end_line": 4, "quoted_text": "Target population: all 96 scheduled coastal stations in the survey network."}, {"path": "results/report.md", "start_line": 8, "end_line": 11, "quoted_text": "Scheduled stations (planned units): 96\nStations passing the signal screen: 72\nStations omitted by the signal screen: 24\nOccurrences observed among the retained stations: 18"}]}, {"description": "The selected result labels the rate as covering the entire scheduled survey network while using 72 retained stations as the exposure denominator - the exact mismatch between claimed population and denominator population.", "observed_value": "18/72 = 0.25 claimed for the entire network", "source_spans": [{"path": "results/report.md", "start_line": 15, "end_line": 15, "quoted_text": "[selected-result] Occurrence rate for the entire scheduled survey network: 18 occurrences divided by 72 retained stations = 0.25 (25.00 occurrences per 100 stations)."}]}, {"description": "The workflow code defines both counts but interpolates SCREEN_PASSED_STATIONS, not SCHEDULED_STATIONS, into the complete-network selected-result string, showing the mismatch originates in the analysis step rather than in report transcription.", "observed_value": "SCREEN_PASSED_STATIONS (72) used as denominator of the network claim", "source_spans": [{"path": "workflow/analysis.py", "start_line": 6, "end_line": 8, "quoted_text": "SCHEDULED_STATIONS = 96\nSCREEN_PASSED_STATIONS = 72\nOMITTED_STATIONS = 24"}, {"path": "workflow/analysis.py", "start_line": 23, "end_line": 23, "quoted_text": "SELECTED_LINE = f'[selected-result] Occurrence rate for the entire scheduled survey network: {OBSERVED_OCCURRENCES} occurrences divided by {SCREEN_PASSED_STATIONS} retained stations = {SELECTED_RATE_FRACTION} ({SELECTED_RATE_PERCENT} occurrences per 100 stations).' + LF"}]}, {"description": "Row-level data show the screen-omitted stations are themselves scheduled units (scheduled=yes) with occurrence_flag NA, so they belong to the complete domain and were dropped from the denominator only because of the screen.", "observed_value": "omitted rows carry scheduled=yes and occurrence_flag NA", "source_spans": [{"path": "inputs/data.csv", "start_line": 5, "end_line": 5, "quoted_text": "CS-004,North,yes,omitted,screen_fail_low_snr,NA"}, {"path": "inputs/data.csv", "start_line": 97, "end_line": 97, "quoted_text": "CS-096,Outer,yes,omitted,screen_fail_data_gap,NA"}]}], "counterevidence_atoms": [{"description": "The report transparently discloses the denominator as the retained 72, which is the strongest argument that the claim is effectively conditional on the screen; but this line describes the computation only and does not restate the target population, while the adjacent selected-result line still asserts coverage of the entire scheduled network.", "observed_value": "denominator disclosed as retained subset", "source_spans": [{"path": "results/report.md", "start_line": 14, "end_line": 14, "quoted_text": "Exposure denominator: the 72 stations retained after the signal screen."}]}, {"description": "Falsification span: the report states no protocol amendment or approved method deviation exists, so the substitution of the retained-subset denominator is not an authorized redefinition of the estimand.", "observed_value": "no amendment or approved deviation", "source_spans": [{"path": "results/report.md", "start_line": 18, "end_line": 18, "quoted_text": "No protocol amendment and no approved method deviation exists for this analysis."}]}], "falsification_attempt": "I tried to falsify the finding by looking for any statement that makes the reported estimand explicitly conditional on the retained subset, which would place it outside this issue class. The only candidate is the denominator disclosure at results/report.md L0014 ('Exposure denominator: the 72 stations retained after the signal screen.'), but it describes the arithmetic rather than restricting the claim: the target line (L0004) and the selected-result line (L0015) both assert the full 96-station scheduled network, task.md L0001 requires the entire network, and L0018 rules out an approved deviation that could have redefined the target. I also checked whether 72 might actually equal the complete scheduled domain by scanning the 'scheduled' column across inputs/data.csv L0002-L0097; all 96 rows including the screen-omitted ones carry scheduled=yes, so 72 is a strict retained subset. The falsification attempt failed and the mismatch stands.", "cross_case_evidence_used": false, "unresolved_material_questions": [], "self_reported_confidence": "high"}]}